Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add AYANEO SLIDE minimum backlight quirk

The AYANEO SLIDE's firmware reports min_input_signal = 38 through the
ACPI ATIF QUERY_BRIGHTNESS_TRANSFER_CHARACTERISTICS method, which amdgpu
scales to 0x101 * 38 = 9766 of 65535, i.e. a PWM duty floor of ~14.9%.
The panel is capable of going far dimmer, but the driver clamps to that
floor, so the lowest selectable backlight level is still uncomfortably
bright in a dark room.

The panel advertises no AUX/DPCD backlight control (the whole eDP
register block at DPCD 0x700..0x72f reads zero), so PWM is the only
available control path and this floor cannot be worked around by
switching backlight control types.

Apply .min_brightness = 1 so min_input_signal becomes 0, the same
treatment already used for the Steam Deck and Framework panels.

Note: with a floor of 0 a backlight level of 0 turns the panel off.
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_panel_backlight_quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_panel_backlight_quirks.c
@@ -72,12 +72,20 @@
 	{
 		.dmi_match.field = DMI_SYS_VENDOR,
 		.dmi_match.value = "AYANEO",
 		.dmi_match_other.field = DMI_PRODUCT_NAME,
 		.dmi_match_other.value = "AYANEO 3",
 		.quirk = { .brightness_mask = 3, },
+	},
+	/* AYANEO SLIDE: ATIF reports min_input_signal 38 (~15% duty), too bright */
+	{
+		.dmi_match.field = DMI_SYS_VENDOR,
+		.dmi_match.value = "AYANEO",
+		.dmi_match_other.field = DMI_PRODUCT_NAME,
+		.dmi_match_other.value = "SLIDE",
+		.quirk = { .min_brightness = 1, },
 	},
 	{
 		.dmi_match.field = DMI_SYS_VENDOR,
 		.dmi_match.value = "ZOTAC",
 		.dmi_match_other.field = DMI_BOARD_NAME,
 		.dmi_match_other.value = "G0A1W",
